{
    "background_story": "Evelyn was a talented botanist who spent most of her life studying the unique properties of flowers. Her fascination with the goldenrod plant, with its vibrant yellow hue and delicate petals, led her to make groundbreaking discoveries about its medicinal properties. Growing up in a small village surrounded by fields of goldenrod, Evelyn developed a deep appreciation for the plant's beauty and resilience. As she delved deeper into her research, she found that the goldenrod held the key to developing new treatments for various ailments. Evelyn's work took her to distant lands, but she always remained connected to her roots, using her knowledge to help those in need and to preserve the natural beauty of the goldenrod fields that inspired her.",
